Search sorted stack maps by bci.

The verifier finds the stack map of a branch target through a cache that
covers the first 512 bytes of a method; past it, it walked every stack map
of the method. Game methods of several kilobytes with hundreds of stack
maps made class loading spend most of the verification time there. When the
method's stack maps have increasing bcis, which populate_stackmap_cache()
now checks, search them by bci; otherwise keep the walk.

